1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:04,730
Circle questions on the SAT
come in a handful of patterns.

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,650
A circle's equation.

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:09,010
An arc or a sector.

4
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,699
Radians.

5
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,569
Angles inside a circle.

6
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:14,330
And tangent lines.

7
00:00:14,399 --> 00:00:17,420
Once you know one key
fact for each pattern,

8
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:21,050
these become some of the most
predictable points on the test.

9
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:24,990
The most common mistake
isn't a hard formula.

10
00:00:25,010 --> 00:00:29,949
It's a small slip at the end:
giving r squared instead of r,

11
00:00:29,969 --> 00:00:32,390
the radius when they
asked for the diameter,

12
00:00:32,410 --> 00:00:34,940
or flipping a sign on the center.

13
00:00:35,090 --> 00:00:39,110
We'll fix all of that, then work through
seven practice questions that get

14
00:00:39,130 --> 00:00:40,660
harder as we go.

15
00:00:41,086 --> 00:00:42,986
Start with the equation of a circle.

16
00:00:43,006 --> 00:00:47,146
In standard form, it's x minus h, squared,

17
00:00:47,166 --> 00:00:50,666
plus y minus k, squared, equals r squared.

18
00:00:50,686 --> 00:00:56,176
The center is the point
h, k, and r is the radius.

19
00:00:56,686 --> 00:00:57,906
Two things to watch.

20
00:00:57,926 --> 00:00:59,866
First, the signs flip.

21
00:00:59,886 --> 00:01:04,866
If you see x minus three, the center's
x coordinate is positive three.

22
00:01:04,886 --> 00:01:09,026
If you see y plus five, the y
coordinate is negative five,

23
00:01:09,046 --> 00:01:13,296
because y plus five is the
same as y minus negative five.

24
00:01:13,795 --> 00:01:17,534
Second, the right side
is r squared, not r.

25
00:01:17,554 --> 00:01:20,855
Here it's thirty-six,
so the radius is six.

26
00:01:20,875 --> 00:01:23,615
If thirty-six shows up as
a choice for the radius,

27
00:01:23,635 --> 00:01:24,635
it's a trap.

28
00:01:25,145 --> 00:01:27,435
Next, arcs and sectors.

29
00:01:27,745 --> 00:01:30,885
An arc is a piece of the circle's edge.

30
00:01:30,905 --> 00:01:35,075
A sector is a slice of the
circle, like a slice of pizza.

31
00:01:35,185 --> 00:01:37,165
You don't need new formulas for either.

32
00:01:37,185 --> 00:01:41,555
You need one idea: what fraction
of the circle do you have?

33
00:01:42,045 --> 00:01:45,705
That fraction is the central
angle over three hundred sixty.

34
00:01:45,725 --> 00:01:48,985
Multiply it by the
circumference for arc length,

35
00:01:49,005 --> 00:01:50,945
or by the area for sector area.

36
00:01:50,965 --> 00:01:54,465
A ninety degree angle is
one fourth of the circle,

37
00:01:54,485 --> 00:01:57,815
so its arc is one fourth
of the circumference.

38
00:01:58,338 --> 00:02:01,028
Radians are just another unit for angles.

39
00:02:01,217 --> 00:02:06,198
The reference sheet tells you a full
circle is three hundred sixty degrees,

40
00:02:06,218 --> 00:02:08,158
or two pi radians.

41
00:02:08,178 --> 00:02:11,788
So one hundred eighty
degrees equals pi radians.

42
00:02:12,058 --> 00:02:16,868
To convert degrees to radians,
multiply by pi over one eighty.

43
00:02:16,888 --> 00:02:20,178
To go back, multiply
by one eighty over pi.

44
00:02:20,709 --> 00:02:25,359
In radians, the fraction of the
circle is the angle over two pi.

45
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:30,559
And there's a shortcut: arc length
equals the radius times the angle.

46
00:02:30,630 --> 00:02:35,118
That shortcut only works in
radians, never in degrees.

47
00:02:35,562 --> 00:02:36,972
Now angles.

48
00:02:37,202 --> 00:02:40,612
A central angle has its
vertex at the center.

49
00:02:40,682 --> 00:02:45,332
An inscribed angle has its
vertex on the circle itself.

50
00:02:45,442 --> 00:02:48,451
When the two angles
open onto the same arc,

51
00:02:48,602 --> 00:02:52,012
the inscribed angle is
half the central angle.

52
00:02:52,501 --> 00:02:53,711
Last fact.

53
00:02:53,981 --> 00:02:58,241
A tangent line touches the
circle at exactly one point,

54
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:02,001
and it's perpendicular to the
radius drawn to that point.

55
00:03:02,021 --> 00:03:04,841
That right angle is the whole trick.

56
00:03:04,861 --> 00:03:08,321
It gives you a right triangle
for the Pythagorean theorem,

57
00:03:08,341 --> 00:03:11,591
or a negative reciprocal slope on a graph.

58
00:03:12,049 --> 00:03:14,629
Here's how to recognize
which fact you need.

59
00:03:14,649 --> 00:03:18,349
If you see x squared and y
squared in the same equation,

60
00:03:18,369 --> 00:03:21,778
it's a circle, and they want
the center or the radius.

61
00:03:21,809 --> 00:03:24,188
If the equation is expanded and messy,

62
00:03:24,208 --> 00:03:26,219
you'll complete the square.

63
00:03:26,647 --> 00:03:29,866
If you see arc, sector,
or part of a circle,

64
00:03:29,886 --> 00:03:31,667
write the fraction first.

65
00:03:31,687 --> 00:03:34,987
If you see radians, or
pi next to an angle,

66
00:03:35,007 --> 00:03:37,577
use one eighty degrees equals pi.

67
00:03:38,007 --> 00:03:40,747
If an angle's vertex sits on the circle,

68
00:03:40,767 --> 00:03:42,136
think half.

69
00:03:42,247 --> 00:03:45,577
And if you see the word
tangent, draw the right angle.

70
00:03:45,996 --> 00:03:47,086
Question one.

71
00:03:47,356 --> 00:03:51,856
In the x y plane, a circle
has the equation x plus four,

72
00:03:51,876 --> 00:03:56,126
squared, plus y minus one,
squared, equals forty-nine.

73
00:03:56,395 --> 00:03:59,686
What are the center and
the radius of the circle?

74
00:04:00,157 --> 00:04:01,807
Pause and try it.

75
00:04:07,593 --> 00:04:08,883
Flip the signs.

76
00:04:09,033 --> 00:04:13,683
x plus four means the center's
x coordinate is negative four.

77
00:04:13,713 --> 00:04:17,333
y minus one means the y
coordinate is positive one.

78
00:04:17,353 --> 00:04:21,363
And forty-nine is r squared,
so the radius is seven.

79
00:04:21,513 --> 00:04:23,322
The answer is A.

80
00:04:23,738 --> 00:04:26,227
B gets the signs backwards.

81
00:04:26,338 --> 00:04:29,908
C and D use forty-nine as the radius.

82
00:04:29,938 --> 00:04:33,227
Those are the two slips this
question is fishing for.

83
00:04:33,636 --> 00:04:34,736
Question two.

84
00:04:34,756 --> 00:04:37,846
A circle has a radius of nine centimeters.

85
00:04:38,076 --> 00:04:42,365
An arc of the circle has a
central angle of eighty degrees.

86
00:04:42,516 --> 00:04:45,726
What is the length of
the arc, in centimeters?

87
00:04:46,135 --> 00:04:47,785
Pause and try it.

88
00:04:53,570 --> 00:04:55,509
Write the fraction first.

89
00:04:55,529 --> 00:04:59,390
Eighty over three sixty
simplifies to two ninths.

90
00:04:59,410 --> 00:05:03,940
The full circumference is two
pi r, which is eighteen pi.

91
00:05:04,250 --> 00:05:06,949
Two ninths of eighteen pi is four pi.

92
00:05:06,969 --> 00:05:08,540
The answer is B.

93
00:05:09,025 --> 00:05:11,715
Eighteen pi is the whole circumference.

94
00:05:11,744 --> 00:05:15,685
Two pi comes from using
pi r instead of two pi r.

95
00:05:15,705 --> 00:05:20,564
And seven twenty is what you get if you
multiply the radius by eighty degrees.

96
00:05:20,584 --> 00:05:23,834
Remember, that shortcut
only works in radians.

97
00:05:24,299 --> 00:05:25,399
Question three.

98
00:05:25,419 --> 00:05:29,029
An angle has a measure of
two hundred ten degrees.

99
00:05:29,339 --> 00:05:32,959
The measure of the angle
in radians is k pi,

100
00:05:32,979 --> 00:05:34,758
where k is a constant.

101
00:05:34,778 --> 00:05:36,708
What is the value of k?

102
00:05:37,191 --> 00:05:38,841
Pause and try it.

103
00:05:44,627 --> 00:05:46,957
Multiply by pi over one eighty.

104
00:05:47,147 --> 00:05:51,647
Two hundred ten times pi over one
eighty is two ten over one eighty,

105
00:05:51,667 --> 00:05:52,367
times pi.

106
00:05:52,387 --> 00:05:57,196
Divide both numbers by thirty,
and that's seven sixths pi.

107
00:05:57,307 --> 00:05:59,757
So k is seven sixths.

108
00:05:59,987 --> 00:06:01,637
Enter it as a fraction.

109
00:06:02,061 --> 00:06:05,840
Sense check: two hundred ten
degrees is a bit more than pi,

110
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:08,081
so k should be a bit more than one.

111
00:06:08,101 --> 00:06:11,151
If you got six sevenths,
you flipped the conversion.

112
00:06:11,604 --> 00:06:12,544
Question four.

113
00:06:12,564 --> 00:06:17,054
Points A, B, and C lie on
a circle with center O.

114
00:06:17,484 --> 00:06:21,743
Angle A O B measures
one hundred ten degrees,

115
00:06:21,763 --> 00:06:25,454
and point C is not on minor arc A B.

116
00:06:25,603 --> 00:06:28,734
What is the measure of angle A C B?

117
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:30,870
Pause and try it.

118
00:06:37,656 --> 00:06:41,636
Angle A O B has its vertex at the center,

119
00:06:41,656 --> 00:06:43,476
so it's a central angle.

120
00:06:43,496 --> 00:06:47,556
Angle A C B has its vertex on the circle,

121
00:06:47,576 --> 00:06:49,076
so it's inscribed.

122
00:06:49,096 --> 00:06:52,916
Both open onto the same arc, arc A B.

123
00:06:52,936 --> 00:06:57,996
So the inscribed angle is half:
half of one ten is fifty-five.

124
00:06:58,016 --> 00:06:59,946
The answer is C.

125
00:07:00,391 --> 00:07:02,251
One twenty-five is the sneaky trap.

126
00:07:02,271 --> 00:07:05,051
That's the angle you'd get
if C were on the minor arc:

127
00:07:05,071 --> 00:07:07,921
half of three sixty minus one ten.

128
00:07:07,991 --> 00:07:11,361
The question rules that out,
so always check where C is.

129
00:07:11,794 --> 00:07:13,124
Now the harder ones.

130
00:07:13,314 --> 00:07:14,653
Question five.

131
00:07:14,673 --> 00:07:20,333
The equation x squared plus y squared
minus ten x plus four y equals twenty

132
00:07:20,353 --> 00:07:23,203
represents a circle in the x y plane.

133
00:07:23,273 --> 00:07:25,324
What is the diameter of the circle?

134
00:07:25,787 --> 00:07:27,437
Pause and try it.

135
00:07:34,223 --> 00:07:37,352
The equation is expanded,
so complete the square.

136
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:40,633
Group the x terms and the y terms.

137
00:07:40,943 --> 00:07:43,483
Half of negative ten is negative five,

138
00:07:43,503 --> 00:07:46,313
and negative five squared is twenty-five.

139
00:07:46,503 --> 00:07:50,833
Half of four is two,
and two squared is four.

140
00:07:50,983 --> 00:07:54,153
Add twenty-five and four to both sides.

141
00:07:54,673 --> 00:07:59,853
That gives x minus five,
squared, plus y plus two,

142
00:07:59,873 --> 00:08:01,733
squared, equals forty-nine.

143
00:08:01,753 --> 00:08:03,683
The radius is seven.

144
00:08:04,312 --> 00:08:06,533
But the question asks for the diameter,

145
00:08:06,553 --> 00:08:08,562
which is twice the radius.

146
00:08:08,672 --> 00:08:09,613
Fourteen.

147
00:08:09,633 --> 00:08:11,283
The answer is B.

148
00:08:11,728 --> 00:08:13,228
Look at the wrong choices.

149
00:08:13,248 --> 00:08:14,947
Seven is the radius.

150
00:08:14,967 --> 00:08:17,218
Forty-nine is r squared.

151
00:08:17,368 --> 00:08:21,828
Four root five is what you get if you
skip completing the square and treat

152
00:08:21,848 --> 00:08:23,828
twenty as r squared.

153
00:08:23,848 --> 00:08:27,098
Every wrong answer is one missed step.

154
00:08:27,550 --> 00:08:31,639
Desmos check: type the equation
exactly as it's written.

155
00:08:31,710 --> 00:08:35,769
Desmos graphs the circle, and
you can read it off the grid.

156
00:08:35,789 --> 00:08:39,730
It runs from x equals negative
two to x equals twelve.

157
00:08:39,750 --> 00:08:41,560
That's fourteen across.

158
00:08:42,043 --> 00:08:43,413
Question six.

159
00:08:43,563 --> 00:08:47,383
In the x y plane, a circle has center two,

160
00:08:47,403 --> 00:08:50,142
negative one, and passes
through the point five,

161
00:08:50,162 --> 00:08:51,063
three.

162
00:08:51,083 --> 00:08:55,943
Which equation represents the line
tangent to the circle at the point five,

163
00:08:55,963 --> 00:08:56,963
three?

164
00:08:57,148 --> 00:08:58,798
Pause and try it.

165
00:09:06,583 --> 00:09:09,243
Tangent means perpendicular to the radius.

166
00:09:09,263 --> 00:09:12,563
So find the radius's slope first.

167
00:09:12,583 --> 00:09:16,122
From two, negative one to five, three,

168
00:09:16,142 --> 00:09:20,042
y goes up four and x goes up three.

169
00:09:20,062 --> 00:09:23,033
The radius has a slope of four thirds.

170
00:09:23,383 --> 00:09:26,083
The tangent's slope is
the negative reciprocal:

171
00:09:26,103 --> 00:09:27,633
negative three fourths.

172
00:09:28,115 --> 00:09:30,255
Now use the point five, three.

173
00:09:30,275 --> 00:09:36,245
y minus three equals negative
three fourths times x minus five.

174
00:09:36,354 --> 00:09:39,494
Multiply both sides by four and rearrange,

175
00:09:39,514 --> 00:09:43,924
and you get three x plus
four y equals twenty-seven.

176
00:09:44,195 --> 00:09:46,245
The answer is D.

177
00:09:46,672 --> 00:09:48,611
Each trap misses one piece.

178
00:09:48,631 --> 00:09:51,372
A is the line through the radius itself.

179
00:09:51,392 --> 00:09:56,172
B has the right slope, but it goes
through the center instead of the point.

180
00:09:56,192 --> 00:10:00,842
C uses negative four thirds, a
negative sign without the reciprocal.

181
00:10:01,276 --> 00:10:05,336
Desmos shortcut: graph
the circle, x minus two,

182
00:10:05,356 --> 00:10:10,605
squared, plus y plus one,
squared, equals twenty-five,

183
00:10:10,755 --> 00:10:12,536
then graph each choice.

184
00:10:12,556 --> 00:10:17,165
Only one line touches the
circle at exactly one point.

185
00:10:17,592 --> 00:10:20,002
Last one, and the hardest.

186
00:10:20,431 --> 00:10:27,092
A circle in the x y plane has the equation
x squared plus y squared minus six x

187
00:10:27,112 --> 00:10:29,642
plus four y equals twenty-three.

188
00:10:29,952 --> 00:10:35,292
A sector of this circle has a central
angle of two pi over three radians.

189
00:10:35,312 --> 00:10:37,402
What is the area of the sector?

190
00:10:37,834 --> 00:10:38,774
Pause and try it.

191
00:10:38,794 --> 00:10:40,443
Take a little longer on this one.

192
00:10:49,253 --> 00:10:50,303
Two steps.

193
00:10:51,013 --> 00:10:53,313
First, find the radius.

194
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:59,392
Complete the square: add nine for
the x terms and four for the y terms.

195
00:10:59,412 --> 00:11:02,953
The right side becomes
twenty-three plus nine plus four,

196
00:11:02,973 --> 00:11:04,582
which is thirty-six.

197
00:11:04,773 --> 00:11:09,743
So the radius is six, and the
full area is thirty-six pi.

198
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:12,530
Second, the fraction.

199
00:11:12,679 --> 00:11:15,650
In radians, the whole circle is two pi.

200
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,339
Two pi over three, divided by two pi,

201
00:11:18,359 --> 00:11:19,739
is one third.

202
00:11:19,759 --> 00:11:22,659
One third of thirty-six pi is twelve pi.

203
00:11:22,679 --> 00:11:24,290
The answer is C.

204
00:11:24,752 --> 00:11:28,772
Four pi is the arc length,
radius times angle,

205
00:11:28,792 --> 00:11:30,122
not the area.

206
00:11:30,192 --> 00:11:35,532
Twenty-four pi treats the whole circle
as pi radians instead of two pi.

207
00:11:35,552 --> 00:11:39,131
And thirty-six pi is the entire circle.

208
00:11:39,151 --> 00:11:41,612
So once again, reread what they ask for.

209
00:11:41,632 --> 00:11:43,362
Arc or area?

210
00:11:43,803 --> 00:11:46,653
Here's the checklist
for any circle question.

211
00:11:46,963 --> 00:11:47,972
Equation?

212
00:11:48,203 --> 00:11:51,343
Get it into standard form, flip the signs,

213
00:11:51,363 --> 00:11:52,773
and take the square root.

214
00:11:53,163 --> 00:11:54,823
Arc or sector?

215
00:11:54,843 --> 00:11:56,653
Write the fraction first.

216
00:11:56,882 --> 00:11:57,903
Radians?

217
00:11:57,923 --> 00:12:00,293
One eighty degrees equals pi.

218
00:12:00,683 --> 00:12:01,903
Angle on the circle?

219
00:12:01,923 --> 00:12:03,423
Half the central angle.

220
00:12:03,443 --> 00:12:04,243
Tangent?

221
00:12:04,263 --> 00:12:06,193
Right angle with the radius.

222
00:12:06,636 --> 00:12:11,206
And before you click, reread
the last line of the question.

223
00:12:11,356 --> 00:12:13,376
Radius or diameter.

224
00:12:13,396 --> 00:12:15,246
Arc or area.

225
00:12:15,316 --> 00:12:19,926
That final check is where most
circle points are won or lost.

226
00:12:20,383 --> 00:12:24,963
For more practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter for

227
00:12:24,983 --> 00:12:28,113
circles under Geometry and Trigonometry.

228
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:32,160
Every question in this video
was written for this video,

229
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:35,150
in the style of the real test.

230
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:38,430
Next up: exponential growth and decay.

231
00:12:38,460 --> 00:12:40,870
If this helped, subscribe so you catch it.
